From: Radxa allwinner-bsp (unmodified), packaged by OctaneOS
Subject: [PATCH] Radxa allwinner-bsp v1.5.0: drivers/drm (display and DisplayPort)

Source:  https://github.com/radxa/allwinner-bsp
Base:    branch cubie-aiot-v1.4.8 @ f9a496c24bf6b7cc31c4b5c716ece58b2c287f01
         (what scripts/setup-kernel-66.sh clones into bsp/)
New:     branch cubie-aiot-v1.5.0 @ 6d5e93bf106ceb6591c49e0ddd2273881e58de56
         (tag aiot-linux-v1.5.0, released 2026-07-15, plus later fixes)
Scope:   only files under drivers/drm that differ between the two branches (36 files:
         DisplayPort controller and driver, display engine, HDMI, bridges, new DP HDCP
         files, Kconfig/Makefile). The GPU (pvr), Wi-Fi and everything else stay on v1.4.8.
Why:     v1.5.0 enables the DP transmitter output before link training, enables
         scrambling when setting the training pattern, reworks hotplug (HPD) handling and
         adds runtime suspend/resume of the DP output. OctaneOS saw link training
         failures at 5.4 Gbps, display blackouts the kernel never noticed, and a black
         screen after the monitor sleeps; see docs/ and the 2026-10 display notes.
License: each file keeps its own SPDX header (GPL-2.0 or GPL-2.0-or-later).
Regenerate: fetch both versions of every file listed below from the two branches and
         run git diff; the files are exactly those GitHub's compare view lists under drivers/drm.
Patch-Source: generated by git diff from complete files (end-of-file hunks may have short context)
---
